  "body": "The existing runtime executes the Phase 1A smoke graph. This adds an injectable canonical sixteen-step graph to the same adapter and PostgresSaver, with reference-only typed state, authorized thin service-port nodes, typed routing, durable human review, canonical events and bounded retry/timeout/step guards. The default smoke graph remains preserved.\n\nPresentation locale is now an optional non-checkpointed RuntimeContext hint for zh-CN / zh-HK / en-US. It is excluded from execution identity and stage requests/results. Canonical event status/reason validation rejects localized semantics. Twenty-five new locale tests compare routing, state/result references, stage requests and event codes. Four PostgreSQL review/restart scenarios additionally switch locales and verify unchanged checkpoint position, snapshot columns and duplicate-delivery behavior.\n\nNo Phase 1I/1J legal implementations or competing authoritative domain contracts are introduced. Unconfigured stages stop with CAPABILITY_NOT_CONFIGURED; the real Phase 1H ClassificationService bridge is available as an explicit application binding. This is Phase 1L-A skeleton only.\n\nValidation:\n- Final implementation head: `39be101e565fa4966e834180523f6ba47a96e5fc`.\n- Local full unchanged fresh-DB gate: 329 passed; zero failures/errors/skips/deselections; architecture 118/118; runtime 25/25; Phase 1H schema 20/20.\n- Exact-head remote run [37271714040](https://github.com/bensuen0831/crossborder-compliance-agent/actions/runs/37271714040): **SUCCESS** on the exact final head. Measured annotation confirms 329 passed, zero failures/errors/skips/deselections, architecture 118/118, runtime 25/25 and Alembic head 0008_phase1h; runner checkout SHA equals the tested head. Artifact metadata was read, but archive digests were not independently recomputed.\n- Verified baseline ancestry: `700951ebb9ebdf33e399158fd3fb53bb4a6c87e7`, tag v3.6-phase1h-pass; no Alembic or ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md changes. Head remains 0008_phase1h.\n- Ruff for new Python and modified event/runtime-context files, and git diff --check, pass.\n\nAll thirteen delivery documents remain in `docs/phase1l_a/`, including design, measured test results and the integration handoff. Local empirical evidence is explicitly working-tree validation; historical pre-locale remote evidence is labeled separately. Shared files for parallel-track coordination: application/ports.py, workflows/langgraph_adapter.py, workflows/runtime_context.py, workflows/events.py, persistence/runtime_operations.py and persistence/repositories.py. Owning services must enforce deadlines and durable idempotency; arbitrary synchronous calls cannot be hard-preempted by this skeleton.\n\nKeep this PR DRAFT targeting main. Do not merge or start Phase 1L-B, full Phase 1L or Phase 1M.\n",
